Can you call a future from a future?

No.

System.AsyncException: Future method cannot be called from a future or batch method.

Same restriction applies to calling a future from Batch Apex execute(). The reason is queue-flooding protection — unbounded self-chaining would let one transaction spawn arbitrary async work.

Workarounds:

Queueable chaining — call System.enqueueJob() from inside a Queueable's execute(). One child job per parent, chain depth unlimited in production (capped at 5 in Developer/Trial orgs). This is the standard answer.
Batch finish() — can enqueue a Queueable or start another batch job.
Scheduled Apex — System.scheduleBatch() or a schedulable that kicks off the next step.

If an interviewer asks this, the follow-up is almost always "so how do you chain async work?" — lead with Queueable.

